<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2" xmlns:gx="http://www.google.com/kml/ext/2.2" xmlns:kml="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom">
<Folder>
	<name>plate_boundaries</name>
	<visibility>0</visibility>
	<Folder>
		<name>sandwell_ridges</name>
		<visibility>0</visibility>
		<description>Digitized ridges and transform faults for mature spreading ridge plate boundaries.  These ridges were digitized to investigate ridge segmentation versus spreading rate.  Offsets in the ridge include any first and second order discontunities as defined by MacDonald et al., [1988].  The 12 segments are defined according to the present-day plate boundaries of DeMets et al., [1994]. The following data were used to estimate the locations of the ridges and offets.  (1) previous digitized ridges by Small and Sandwell [1992],  Bird et al., [2003], and the USGS.  (2) replcated shallow earthquakes magnitude &gt; 5.4 [Engdahl et al., 1997]. (3) Vertical gravity gradient from satellite altimetry [Sandwell and Smith, 2008]. (4) Measured seafloor depth from Becker et al., [2009].</description>
